{"course": {"id": "s15", "title": "Camday – Cambridge Primary Mathematics — Stage 5", "units": [{"n": 1, "t": "The Number System"}, {"n": 2, "t": "2D Shapes"}, {"n": 3, "t": "Numbers and Sequences"}, {"n": 4, "t": "Averages"}, {"n": 5, "t": "Addition and Subtraction (1)"}, {"n": 6, "t": "3D Shapes"}, {"n": 7, "t": "Fractions, Decimals and Percentages"}, {"n": 8, "t": "Probability"}, {"n": 9, "t": "Addition and Subtraction (2)"}, {"n": 10, "t": "Angles"}, {"n": 11, "t": "Multiplication and Division"}, {"n": 12, "t": "Data"}, {"n": 13, "t": "Ratio and Proportion"}, {"n": 14, "t": "Area and Perimeter"}, {"n": 15, "t": "Multiplying and Dividing Fractions and Decimals"}, {"n": 16, "t": "Time"}, {"n": 17, "t": "Number and the Laws of Arithmetic"}, {"n": 18, "t": "Position and Direction"}]}, "unit": {"n": 4, "stage": 15, "title": "Averages", "strandShort": "Statistics and probability", "blurb": "Finding the mode and the median of a set of data, and using them to describe and compare data.", "strand": "Statistics and probability", "framework": "Cambridge Primary Mathematics (0096), Stage 5", "lesson": true, "subject": "maths", "read": "media/read/m5u04.pdf"}, "objectives": {"O1": {"code": "5Ss.03", "sec": "4.1", "codeNote": "", "t": "Find and interpret the mode of a set of data, including data with no mode or more than one mode."}, "O2": {"code": "5Ss.04", "sec": "4.2", "codeNote": "", "t": "Find and interpret the median of a set of data."}}, "sections": [{"id": "4.1", "title": "The mode", "objs": ["O1"], "lesson": [{"k": "hook", "t": "Shoe shop order", "p": ["A shop sold these trainer sizes on Saturday: **4, 5, 5, 6, 5, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7**.", "The manager can only order more of **one** size. Which size should she choose? Think about it before you read on."]}, {"k": "recall", "t": "Tally charts", "p": ["Count how many times each value appears."], "qq": {"id": "m5u04s1t01", "type": "num", "prompt": "How many times does 5 appear in 4, 5, 5, 6, 5?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 3, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": "3."}}, {"k": "idea", "t": "The mode", "p": ["The **mode** is the value that appears **most often**."], "table": {"head": ["Size", "3", "4", "5", "6", "7"], "rows": [["Frequency", "1", "2", "4", "2", "1"]]}, "fig": {"kind": "barchart", "labels": ["3", "4", "5", "6", "7"], "values": [1, 2, 4, 2, 1], "ymax": 5, "step": 1, "ylabel": "Pairs sold"}, "p2": ["The mode is size **5** – order more of that."]}, {"k": "idea", "t": "More than one mode, or none", "p": ["If two values are equally most common, there are **two modes** (e.g. 2, 2, 3, 3, 4 → modes 2 and 3).", "If every value appears once, there is **no mode**.", "The mode works for words too: the modal colour, modal pet."]}, {"k": "try", "t": "Mode", "p": [], "qq": {"id": "m5u04s1t02", "type": "num", "prompt": "Mode of 7, 3, 7, 1, 2, 7, 3?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 7, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": "7."}}, {"k": "method", "t": "How do I find the mode?", "p": ["Step 1: Count how often each value appears (tally or table).", "Step 2: Find the highest frequency.", "Step 3: The value(s) with it are the mode(s).", "Step 4: If all appear once, there is no mode."]}, {"k": "example", "t": "Words", "p": [], "q": "Pets: dog, cat, fish, dog, cat, dog.", "steps": [["dog 3, cat 2, fish 1", ""]], "a": "dog"}, {"k": "example", "t": "Two modes", "p": [], "q": "Scores 8, 9, 8, 10, 9.", "steps": [["8 twice, 9 twice", ""]], "a": "8 and 9"}, {"k": "example", "t": "From a bar chart", "p": [], "q": "Bars: red 6, blue 9, green 4.", "steps": [["tallest bar: blue", ""]], "a": "blue"}, {"k": "example", "t": "No mode", "p": [], "q": "1, 2, 3, 4, 5.", "steps": [["each once", ""]], "a": "no mode"}, {"k": "try", "t": "Words", "p": [], "qq": {"id": "m5u04s1t03", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "Mode of: bus, car, walk, car, bike, car?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "hint": "", "reason": "", "options": [{"t": "car", "ok": true, "fb": ""}, {"t": "bus", "ok": false, "fb": ""}]}}, {"k": "error", "t": "Gave the frequency", "p": ["Find the first wrong line."], "q": "Mode of the shoe sizes.", "lines": ["size 5 appears 4 times, so the mode is 4"], "bad": 0, "why": "The mode is the VALUE (size 5), not how many times it appears.", "fix": [["mode = 5", ""]], "id": "m5u04s1t04"}, {"k": "mistake", "t": "Giving the frequency instead of the value", "p": ["The mode is the most common value."]}, {"k": "tip", "t": "Real life", "p": ["Shops use the mode to decide which sizes and flavours to stock most."]}, {"k": "summary", "t": "What to remember", "p": ["Mode = most common value.", "There can be two modes, or none.", "Works for words and numbers.", "Tallest bar = mode."]}], "video": {"src": null, "offset": 0, "dur": 660, "range": ""}, "stops": [{"id": "4.1-k1", "t": 1, "after": 0, "review": [0, 0], "note": "", "q": {"id": "m5u04s1k01", "type": "num", "prompt": "Before you read on: size to order?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 5, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}}, {"id": "4.1-k2", "t": 2, "after": 4, "review": [0, 0], "note": "", "q": {"id": "m5u04s1k02", "type": "num", "prompt": "How many pairs of size 4?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 2, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}}, {"id": "4.1-k3", "t": 3, "after": 9, "review": [0, 0], "note": "", "q": {"id": "m5u04s1k03", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "2, 2, 3, 3, 4 has …", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "hint": "", "reason": "", "options": [{"t": "two modes", "ok": true, "fb": ""}, {"t": "no mode", "ok": false, "fb": ""}]}}, {"id": "4.1-k4", "t": 4, "after": 14, "review": [0, 0], "note": "", "q": {"id": "m5u04s1k04", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "Quick check: 1, 2, 3 has …", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "hint": "", "reason": "", "options": [{"t": "no mode", "ok": true, "fb": ""}, {"t": "mode 2", "ok": false, "fb": ""}]}}], "captions": [], "chapters": [[0, 300]], "req": [{"id": "m5u04s1r01", "type": "num", "prompt": "Mode of 4, 6, 4, 8?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 4, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m5u04s1r02", "type": "num", "prompt": "Mode of 10, 12, 12, 11, 12?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 12, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m5u04s1r03", "type": "num", "prompt": "Mode of 3, 3, 3, 5, 5?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 3, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m5u04s1r04", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "Mode of red, blue, red, green?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "hint": "", "reason": "", "options": [{"t": "red", "ok": true, "fb": ""}, {"t": "blue", "ok": false, "fb": ""}]}, {"id": "m5u04s1r05", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "2, 4, 6, 8 has …", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "hint": "", "reason": "", "options": [{"t": "no mode", "ok": true, "fb": ""}, {"t": "mode 4", "ok": false, "fb": ""}]}, {"id": "m5u04s1r06", "type": "num", "prompt": "Bars: A 3, B 7, C 5. Frequency of the mode?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 7, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m5u04s1r07", "type": "num", "prompt": "Mode of 0.5, 1, 0.5, 2?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 0.5, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m5u04s1r08", "type": "num", "prompt": "Mode of 9, 8, 9, 7, 8, 9?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 9, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}], "prac": [{"id": "m5u04s1p01", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "Modes of 1, 1, 2, 2, 3?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "hint": "", "reason": "", "options": [{"t": "1 and 2", "ok": true, "fb": ""}, {"t": "2", "ok": false, "fb": ""}]}, {"id": "m5u04s1p02", "type": "num", "prompt": "Add one number to 5, 6, 6, 7, 7 so the mode is 7. Number?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 7, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m5u04s1p03", "type": "num", "prompt": "Goals in matches: 0, 2, 1, 2, 3, 2, 0. Mode?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 2, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m5u04s1p04", "type": "explain", "prompt": "Explain why a shoe shop finds the mode more useful than other averages.", "diff": "H", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "rubric": [{"pt": "most popular size", "kw": ["most|popular|common|sells"]}], "need": 1, "model": "The mode is the most popular size, which tells the shop what to stock most.", "hint": "", "reason": "The mode is the most popular size, which tells the shop what to stock most."}, {"id": "m5u04s1p05", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "Mode of letters in BANANA?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "hint": "", "reason": "", "options": [{"t": "A", "ok": true, "fb": ""}, {"t": "N", "ok": false, "fb": ""}]}, {"id": "m5u04s1p06", "type": "num", "prompt": "Dice rolls 3, 5, 2, 5, 6, 1, 5, 4. Mode?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 5, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m5u04s1p07", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "Can the mode be a word?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "hint": "", "reason": "", "options": [{"t": "Yes", "ok": true, "fb": ""}, {"t": "No", "ok": false, "fb": ""}]}, {"id": "m5u04s1p08", "type": "num", "prompt": "Ages 9, 10, 10, 11, 9, 10. Mode?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 10, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}], "adv": [{"id": "m5u04s1a01", "type": "explain", "prompt": "* Advanced. Write 5 numbers with mode 4 where 4 is also the largest number.", "diff": "H", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "rubric": [{"pt": "example", "kw": ["4.*4"]}], "need": 1, "model": "e.g. 1, 2, 4, 4, 4.", "hint": "", "reason": "e.g. 1, 2, 4, 4, 4."}, {"id": "m5u04s1a02", "type": "num", "prompt": "* Advanced. 6 numbers: 2, 3, 3, 5, 5, x. The mode is 5 only. x?", "diff": "H", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 5, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m5u04s1a03", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "* Advanced. A data set has 3 modes. What must be true?", "diff": "H", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "hint": "", "reason": "", "options": [{"t": "three values tie for most common", "ok": true, "fb": ""}, {"t": "there are only 3 values", "ok": false, "fb": ""}]}], "more": [{"id": "m5u04s1m01", "type": "num", "prompt": "Mode of 1, 1, 2?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 1, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m5u04s1m02", "type": "num", "prompt": "Mode of 5, 6, 6?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 6, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m5u04s1m03", "type": "num", "prompt": "Mode of 3, 4, 4, 4?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 4, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m5u04s1m04", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "Mode of cat, cat, dog?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "hint": "", "reason": "", "options": [{"t": "cat", "ok": true, "fb": ""}, {"t": "dog", "ok": false, "fb": ""}]}, {"id": "m5u04s1m05", "type": "num", "prompt": "Mode of 2, 7, 7, 9?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 7, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m5u04s1m06", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "Mode means …", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "hint": "", "reason": "", "options": [{"t": "most common", "ok": true, "fb": ""}, {"t": "middle", "ok": false, "fb": ""}]}], "notes": "v4", "pdf": [{"book": "c5u04", "p0": 2, "p1": 5, "label": "pages 2–5", "title": "Lesson 4.1 notes · The mode", "note": "The whole lesson as a document you can print, then Practice on paper with answers at the back.", "look": []}]}, {"id": "4.2", "title": "The median", "objs": ["O2"], "lesson": [{"k": "hook", "t": "Middle runner", "p": ["Seven children run 100 m. Their times (seconds): **18, 15, 21, 16, 19, 17, 25**.", "Which time is 'in the middle'? How could you find it? Think about it before you read on."]}, {"k": "recall", "t": "Ordering", "p": ["Order 18, 15, 21: 15, 18, 21."], "qq": {"id": "m5u04s2t01", "type": "num", "prompt": "Smallest of 18, 15, 21, 16, 19, 17, 25?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 15, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": "15."}}, {"k": "idea", "t": "The median", "p": ["The **median** is the **middle value** when the data is **in order**.", "Times in order: 15, 16, 17, **18**, 19, 21, 25. There are 7 values; the 4th is the middle → median **18 s**.", "The very slow 25 s doesn't change the median – it is not affected by one extreme value."]}, {"k": "idea", "t": "An even number of values", "p": ["With an even number of values there are **two middle values**: the median is **halfway between them**."], "table": {"head": ["Data in order", "Middle values", "Median"], "rows": [["3, 5, 8, 10", "5 and 8", "6.5"], ["12, 14, 14, 20", "14 and 14", "14"], ["2, 4, 6, 8, 10, 12", "6 and 8", "7"]]}}, {"k": "try", "t": "Median", "p": [], "qq": {"id": "m5u04s2t02", "type": "num", "prompt": "Median of 9, 3, 6, 2, 8?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 6, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "Order: 2, 3, 6, 8, 9.", "reason": "6."}}, {"k": "method", "t": "How do I find the median?", "p": ["Step 1: Put the data in order.", "Step 2: Cross off one from each end until you reach the middle.", "Step 3: Odd number of values → one middle value.", "Step 4: Even number → halfway between the two middle values."]}, {"k": "example", "t": "Odd", "p": [], "q": "Median of 30, 12, 25, 18, 40.", "steps": [["12, 18, 25, 30, 40", ""], ["middle: 25", ""]], "a": "25"}, {"k": "example", "t": "Even", "p": [], "q": "Median of 7, 1, 4, 10.", "steps": [["1, 4, 7, 10", ""], ["halfway between 4 and 7: 5.5", ""]], "a": "5.5"}, {"k": "example", "t": "Repeated values", "p": [], "q": "Median of 3, 3, 3, 9, 10.", "steps": [["middle: 3", ""]], "a": "3"}, {"k": "example", "t": "Compare with mode", "p": [], "q": "Data 2, 2, 5, 7, 9: mode and median.", "steps": [["mode 2", ""], ["median 5", ""]], "a": "mode 2, median 5"}, {"k": "try", "t": "Even", "p": [], "qq": {"id": "m5u04s2t03", "type": "num", "prompt": "Median of 6, 2, 8, 4?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 5, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "2, 4, 6, 8.", "reason": "5."}}, {"k": "error", "t": "Forgot to order", "p": ["Find the first wrong line."], "q": "Median of 18, 15, 21, 16, 19, 17, 25.", "lines": ["middle of the list as written: 16"], "bad": 0, "why": "Order first: 15, 16, 17, 18, 19, 21, 25 → median 18.", "fix": [["ordered → 18", ""]], "id": "m5u04s2t04"}, {"k": "mistake", "t": "Taking the middle of an unordered list", "p": ["Always order first."]}, {"k": "tip", "t": "Real life", "p": ["House prices and incomes are often described by the median, because a few very large values don't distort it."]}, {"k": "summary", "t": "What to remember", "p": ["Median = middle value in order.", "Order first!", "Even number of values → halfway between the middle two.", "Not changed much by one extreme value."]}], "video": {"src": null, "offset": 0, "dur": 660, "range": ""}, "stops": [{"id": "4.2-k1", "t": 1, "after": 0, "review": [0, 0], "note": "", "q": {"id": "m5u04s2k01", "type": "num", "prompt": "Before you read on: middle time?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 18, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}}, {"id": "4.2-k2", "t": 2, "after": 4, "review": [0, 0], "note": "", "q": {"id": "m5u04s2k02", "type": "num", "prompt": "How many values are on each side of the median of 7 values?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 3, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}}, {"id": "4.2-k3", "t": 3, "after": 9, "review": [0, 0], "note": "", "q": {"id": "m5u04s2k03", "type": "num", "prompt": "Median of 3, 5, 8, 10?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 6.5, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}}, {"id": "4.2-k4", "t": 4, "after": 14, "review": [0, 0], "note": "", "q": {"id": "m5u04s2k04", "type": "num", "prompt": "Quick check: median of 1, 2, 3?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 2, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}}], "captions": [], "chapters": [[0, 300]], "req": [{"id": "m5u04s2r01", "type": "num", "prompt": "Median of 4, 8, 6?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O2", "skill": "Application", "answer": 6, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}, {"id": "m5u04s2r02", "type": "num", "prompt": "Median of 10, 2, 7, 5, 9?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O2", "skill": "Application", "answer": 7, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "